      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I can confirm fallback to standard is not accepting the correct settings ever since the last several recent updates. In my case, the emissions are carried over but to a very high degree where I look very white. Disabling emissions seem to make the fallback work more or less, but I would have to forgo emissions on my default. This was definitely not an issue before and appears to affect anything that doesn't fallback to toon lit. Spent a frustrating amount of time disabling things one at a time, uploading the avatar, switching shader fallback, and just going trial and error to get to the root of my issue.\n\nFor now, I just settle with toon lot as a shader fallback - but it's not my preferred option.\n\nIn my case, my issue started about 2-3 months ago? It was fine for me prior.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
